lightdm (1.32.0-6ubuntu3) plucky; urgency=medium

  * Cherry-pick changes from the previously-held Ubuntu delta, remaining
    delta (LP: #2104169):
    - debian/01_debian.conf: Remove the default greeter session, this is set
      by gsettings.
    - debian/02_ubuntu.conf: Add an Ubuntu-specific configuration:
      + Disable the built-in log backup mechanism in favor of logrotate, the
        configuration for which is defined in debian/lightdm.logrotate.
      + Enable coredumps when running X.
      + Use lightdm-greeter-session for greeter-wrapper, as defined in
        debian/lightdm-greeter-session.
      + Use lightdm-session for session-wrapper, as defined in
        debian/lightdm-session (LP: #2098411).
    - debian/config-error-dialog.sh: Used by lightdm-greeter-session, this
      dialog alerts the user when a configuration value is invalid, instead of
      simply failing.
    - debian/lightdm.install: Install the aforementioned configuration files
      into /etc/lightdm/lightdm.conf.d instead of
      /usr/share/lightdm/lightdm.conf.d for better visibility and
      compatibility.
    - debian/source_lightdm.py: Apport hook.

